WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.538
I believe this is a great opportunity 
for us to bring our own projects,

00:00:15.538 --> 00:00:24.438
and to share these and also compare these
with others involved in the Laboratory

00:00:24.438 --> 00:00:26.763
– all of whom are very qualified.

00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:31.435
This process will help guide my own work

00:00:31.435 --> 00:00:38.200
in a more detailed and precise way.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:47.000
Dramaturgy is a concept
which can not be defined just in one way.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.908
I would say it's quite an open concept

00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:55.948
that you can orientate and build
in different ways.

00:00:55.948 --> 00:01:01.718
We will give a clearer idea
about what a dramaturg can do

00:01:01.718 --> 00:01:06.660
and also, maybe, I hope
that we also get some knowledge

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:14.068
about composition and design structures
of movement, and maybe choreography.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:30.890
It has been inspiring to see the multiple ways
in which people build in dramaturgy

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:35.983
and to be able to pick on the way
they are building their performances,

00:01:35.983 --> 00:01:38.043
their artistic content.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:42.500
It's important that
the participants understand also

00:01:44.045 --> 00:01:48.548
the questions to do to a dramaturg.

00:01:49.468 --> 00:01:54.798
I mean, I have this idea,
how I can spend all my energy

00:01:54.798 --> 00:01:59.877
to express my idea,
so working with tension,

00:01:59.877 --> 00:02:06.377
with time, with movements,
with all the elements of a choreography.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:16.640
I saw they were very interested about
acoustic [audio] description,

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.682
I saw a very theoretical part
about dramaturgy,

00:02:22.682 --> 00:02:26.957
I saw different kinds of things,

00:02:26.957 --> 00:02:35.665
and all those gave me the inspiration
to start looking also by myself a lot of things.

00:02:38.435 --> 00:02:45.518
I can say that I have more knowledge
about what is happening.

